<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Security Assessment Report</title>
<style>
body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 960px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
h1, h2, h3 { border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: .3rem; }
pre { background: #f5f5f5; padding: .8rem; overflow-x: auto; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: .4rem; text-align: left; }
.critical { color: #a00; } .high { color: #c60; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Security Assessment Report</h1>
<p><strong>Target:</strong> {{ state.target.name }} ({{ state.target.base_url }})<br>
<strong>Model backend:</strong> {{ model_label }}<br>
<strong>Started:</strong> {{ state.started_at.isoformat() }}<br>
<strong>Finished:</strong> {{ state.finished_at.isoformat() if state.finished_at else 'in progress' }}<br>
<strong>Attacks executed:</strong> {{ state.tested | length }}</p>

<h2>Executive Summary</h2>
<p>Reconnaissance identified {{ state.surface | length }} capability areas. The agent
tested {{ categories_tested }} vulnerability classes and confirmed
{{ state.findings | length }} findings. Critical {{ counts.critical }},
high {{ counts.high }}, medium {{ counts.medium }}, low {{ counts.low }}.</p>
<p>Methodology: benign reconnaissance mapped the attack surface. Seeded templates and
the configured attacker model produced payloads. Rule-based canary checks and model
judgment classified responses. Each suspected finding was replayed before confirmation.</p>

<h2>Findings</h2>
{% for finding in state.findings %}
<h3>{{ loop.index }}. {{ finding.name }} <span class="{{ finding.severity.value }}">({{ finding.severity.value | upper }})</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Category:</strong> {{ finding.category.value }}</li>
<li><strong>Confidence:</strong> {{ '%.2f' | format(finding.confidence) }}</li>
<li><strong>Description:</strong> {{ finding.description }}</li>
<li><strong>Methodology:</strong> {{ finding.methodology }}</li>
<li><strong>Impact:</strong> {{ finding.impact }}</li>
<li><strong>Remediation:</strong> {{ finding.remediation }}</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Reproduction</strong></p><pre>{{ finding.reproduction }}</pre>
{% for item in evidence_by_finding.get(finding.id, []) %}
<p><strong>Evidence</strong> — {{ item.attack_id }} — {{ item.note }}</p>
<p>Request:</p><pre>{{ item.request | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre>
<p>Response:</p><pre>{{ item.response | tojson(indent=2) }}</pre>
<p>Canary hits: {{ item.canary_hits | join(', ') if item.canary_hits else 'none' }}</p>
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

<h2>Appendix A: Rejected and suspicious attempts</h2>
<table><tr><th>Attack</th><th>Category</th><th>Tactic</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Reason</th></tr>
{% for record in state.tested if record.verdict in ['rejected', 'suspicious'] %}
<tr><td>{{ record.id }}</td><td>{{ record.category.value }}</td><td>{{ record.tactic }}</td><td>{{ record.verdict.value }}</td><td>{{ record.evidence }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>Appendix B: Run metadata</h2>
<p><strong>Budgets:</strong> {{ state.budgets | tojson }}<br>
<strong>Planner decisions:</strong> {{ state.planner_log | length }}<br>
<strong>Evidence items:</strong> {{ state.evidence | length }}<br>
<strong>Scope:</strong> local authorized target only.</p>
</body>
</html>
